t trial, while its per-colony table shows the 24 bouts come from only 8 colonies (3 each), i.e., repeated measurements from the same independent unit entered a row-independent procedure as if independent.\",\"The reported significance (18/24 UV picks, p = 0.0227) is computed with n = 24 trials rather than 8 independent colonies, and the per-colony table shows strong within-colony clustering (five colonies at 3/3, one at 0/3), confirming the correlated rows were treated as free-standing trials.\",\"No authority lock was minted, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"issue","lock_follows_declaration":"not-applicable-no-lock","reasons":["Declared independent-unit column colony_id matches the frozen data: input.csv has 24 rows with labels C01-C08 and exactly three rows per colony, as declared; all rows feed the single binomial-test pathway, so the declaration holds for the whole procedure.","The selected report demonstrates the issue: it states the exact two-sided binomial test was run on 24 bout outcomes with each bout entering as one independent trial, while its per-colony table shows the 24 bouts come from only 8 colonies (3 each), i.e., repeated measurements from the same independent unit entered a row-independent procedure as if independent.","The reported significance (18/24 UV picks, p = 0.0227) is computed with n = 24 trials rather than 8 independent colonies, and the per-colony table shows strong within-colony clustering (five colonies at 3/3, one at 0/3), confirming the correlated rows were treated as free-standing trials.","No authority lock was minted, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock."]},"ttft_ms":5508,"ttft_stream_ms":1795,"time_to_request_ms":13,"type":"result","duration_ms":17160,"uuid":"c35f37f2-4874-4905-a701-f1d8c78b524e"}
